esults.eci.gov.in/PcResultGenJune2024/index.htm"}],"system":{"type":"First-past-the-post in single-member constituencies","elects":"543 members of the Lok Sabha","votingAge":18,"eligibility":"Citizens of India 18+ not otherwise disqualified (Constitution Art. 326)","compulsory":false,"turnoutPct":66.1,"turnoutSource":"https://www.eci.gov.in/eci-backend/public/all_files/GE-2024-statistical-report/2-Heighlights.pdf"},"wildFacts":[{"text":"About 97.98 crore (~980 million) electors were registered, voting at 1,052,664 polling stations.","source":"https://www.eci.gov.in/EBooks/atlas-2024/files/basic-html/page27.html"},{"text":"Surat's seat was decided without a vote: the candidate was elected unopposed.","source":"https://www.eci.gov.in/EBooks/atlas-2024/files/basic-html/page27.html"},{"text":"Karur (Tamil Nadu) had 54 candidates on the ballot; Dhubri (Assam) had the highest turnout at 92.30%.","source":"https://www.eci.gov.in/EBooks/atlas-2024/files/basic-html/page27.html"},{"text":"Tashigang (Himachal Pradesh), at 15,256 ft, was the highest polling station.","source":"https://www.eci.gov.in/EBooks/atlas-2024/files/basic-html/page27.html"},{"text":"The indelible ink marking voters' fingers comes from a single manufacturer, Mysore Paints & Varnish Ltd.","source":"https://indianexpress.com/article/explained/explained-politics/lok-sabha-elections-voting-indelible-ink-9279884/"}],"notes":"Seats are from the ECI final results page (archived copy; 543 of 543 declared). Turnout 66.1% includes postal ballots (65.66% excl. postal; provisional 65.79% per The Hindu). Six states show no winner because no final ECI tally could be found; four regions are tied on seats. Voting age 18 (Constitution Art. 326: https://www.constitutionofindia.net/articles/article-326-elections-to-the-house-of-the-people-and-to-the-legislative-assemblies-of-states-to-be-on-the-basis-of-adult-suffrage/). Voting is not compulsory (International IDEA: https://www.idea.int/data-tools/data/voter-turnout-database/compulsory-voting).","verified":"2026-11-04 04:35 CT","nationalWinner":"Bharatiya Janata Party (largest party, 240 of 543; no single-party majority)"}